FEX: keep x18 out of the JIT's dynamic register pool (Darwin host)
====================================================================

Why: Darwin's kernel zeroes x18 on every exception return -- a raw svc, a
signal, a sleep, and preemption (benchmarks/stage5-x18.txt: 444 losses in
1.5 s of preemption with no syscalls at all). FEX's 64-bit-mode register
allocator hands x18 to guest values (x64::RA, PreserveAll_Dynamic in
FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp), so translated
code silently lost values. The same file already excludes x18 on ARM64EC
(Windows), where it is the TEB pointer.

Which Linux dependency it removes: none. It is a host-platform constraint
(x18 is the platform register on Darwin and Windows; a temporary on Linux).

Upstreamable: yes, as a CMake option or a host-platform check
("reserve x18 when the host is not Linux"); the ARM64EC branch is the
precedent. Cost of one fewer dynamic register: not measured yet.

External alternative: none for JIT output. FEX's own C++ and the guest's
libraries are covered separately: FEX is built with -ffixed-x18 (both
Build/ and Build-dbg/ on the guest: cmake -DCMAKE_C_FLAGS=-ffixed-x18
-DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=-ffixed-x18), and unmodified Linux libraries (glibc 326
sites, libstdc++ 251, ld.so 27, libgcc_s 40, libm 44) get x18 virtualised
by the runtime's rewriter (runtime/x18.c) -- see MIGRATION_PLAN Stage 5.

Maintenance: 12 changed lines in one file; rebase trivially.

Applied on the guest tree at FEX-2609-113-g08f451d3b (commit 08f451d3b).

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/ArchHelpers/Arm64Emitter.cpp
